    - docstring_audit  # 381e
    isbefore: []  # 381e
    duplicate_of: []  # 381e
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 381e
    pr_ref:  # 381e
    description: "Repro: a python overlay with `provenance: community` and a complete module_completeness grant for telnetlib, passed with origin cli or claims_file: catalog_provenance puts telnetlib in completeness_grants (withheld empty) and the text renderer prints 'COMPLETENESS GRANTS ... counts as an EXAMINED negative ... python: telnetlib from comm.yaml [CLI flag]'. With origin config it is withheld. load_catalog(...).module_completeness does not contain telnetlib, so the VERDICT is unaffected; the disclosure is false. The module docstring was reworded to describe the current behaviour in the 2026-10-10 audit PR; revert that wording when fixed.\n\nFound by the 2026-10-10 docstring-staleness audit (reviewer + default-REJECT verifier, reproduced). Notebook: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_10102026.md."  # 381e
    fields:  # 381e
      statement: "catalog_provenance lists every module_completeness grant from a `provenance: community` file under withheld_completeness_grants, whatever path loaded the file (ADR-0061)."  # 381e
      root_cause: "catalog_provenance skips the community check for origins 'cli' and 'claims_file' (verify_claims.py ~2367-2369: `if origin in (\"cli\", \"claims_file\"): continue`), while io_boundary.load_catalog withholds community grants for every origin."  # 381e
