- op: discuss  # 0973
  at: '2026-10-11T08:51:15Z'  # 0973
  by: agent  # 0973
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0973
  clock: 3  # 0973
  nonce: '0973'  # 0973
  message: "Fixed in PR #1533 (merge 51f5b3755f). Root cause: catalog_provenance read --io-primitives and claims-file overlay paths from layers and listed their grants under completeness_grants without asking overlay_declares_community; only config-tier/channel origins were partitioned, while io_boundary.load_catalog withholds community grants for every origin. Fix: one _partition_completeness_grants applied to every origin; the text WITHHELD block now names each file's origin like the applied block; module and catalog_provenance docstrings restored to describe the fixed behaviour. Evidence (live, dev 51f5b3755f, comm.yaml = provenance: community + telnetlib complete grant, repo/main.py writes os.environ to telnetlib.Telnet): 'hypergumbo verify-claims repo --claims claims.yaml --io-primitives comm.yaml' -> rc 2, text shows 'WITHHELD GRANTS ... python: telnetlib / from comm.yaml [CLI flag]' and no COMPLETENESS GRANTS block; --json gives completeness_grants=[] and withheld_completeness_grants=[{origin: cli, modules: [telnetlib], path: comm.yaml}]. Via claims file 'extra_catalogs: io_primitives: [comm.yaml]' -> rc 2, 'WITHHELD GRANTS ... from comm.yaml [claims-file extra_catalogs]'. Before (origin/dev 92c19aeff6 snapshot, same CLI command): rc 2, 'COMPLETENESS GRANTS ... python: telnetlib from comm.yaml [CLI flag]'. Verdict rc unchanged (disclosure-only), as the item stated. Production-path test: test_in_repo_catalogues.py::TestCatalogProvenance::test_a_community_grant_is_withheld_whatever_path_loaded_it[cli|claims_file]."  # 0973
